%N A398497 Irregular triangle read by rows: T(n,k) is the number of rooted binary leaf-labeled simplex time-consistent galled trees with n leaves and exactly k galls, 0 <= k <= floor((n-1)/2).
%C A398497 For fixed k, the asymptotic growth of T(n,k) with increasing n follows T(n,k) ~ (2^(2*k-1) / ((2*k)!*sqrt(Pi))) * n^(2*k - 3/2) * (1/2)^(-n+k) * n! (eq. 64 of Agranat-Tamir et al., Adv. Appl. Math. 180 (2026), 103131).
%H A398497 Lily Agranat-Tamir, Michael Fuchs, Bernhard Gittenberger, Noah A. Rosenberg, and Karthik V. Seetharaman, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1016/j.aam.2026.103131">Combinatorial comparison of general galled trees, time-consistent galled trees, and simplex time-consistent galled trees</a>, Adv. Appl. Math. 180, 103131 (2026). See Table 4.
%F A398497 E.g.f. satisfies A(x,y) = x + (1/2) * A(x,y)^2 + (x*y/2) * (A(x,y) / (1-A(x,y)))^2 (Agranat-Tamir et al., Adv. Appl. Math. 180 (2026), 103131, p. 35).
